Work in the hiyroscript/seren repository on the current main branch.

Objective

Fix a race-simulation bug where racers that are sufficiently far away from Player 1 can effectively stop making race progress when Player 1 is destroyed/wrecked.

Seren is supposed to behave like an actual race simulation: every racer still in the race must have independent longitudinal progress. Destroying the player may stop that player’s car temporarily, but it must never stop, freeze, pause, tether, or otherwise suspend the other racers.

This must be fixed at the simulation/state-model level. Do not hide the problem with a larger coordinate clamp, special-case HUD math, fake catch-up, or by continuing to advance the player’s distance while their car is wrecked.

