Validation

Run the existing relevant regression suites after implementing the change, especially:

node tools/progression-check.mjs

node tools/ultimate-check.mjs

node tools/hitbox-check.mjs

node tools/check.mjs

Also run the other existing Seren checks if the changes touch their domains.

Pay particular attention to Neela’s swap/rebase tests and Rhosyn’s canonical-position tests because both rely heavily on the distinction between world position and presentation.

Finally, manually or deterministically reproduce the original scenario:

* create a racer more than roughly 2.25 km ahead of Player 1;
* make sure it is actively driving;
* destroy Player 1;
* observe Player 1 stop;
* verify the distant racer continues accumulating metres every simulation frame;
* verify standings continue changing;
* verify it can cross the finish line during Player 1’s wreck;
* verify Player 1 respawning does not cause any rival position correction.

Definition of done

The fix is complete when the race simulation no longer depends on Player 1 moving in order for another racer to make forward progress.

A useful final invariant is:

A racer’s race distance is determined by that racer’s own movement, not by whether that racer is visible and not by whether Player 1’s camera is moving.

Player destruction should affect Player 1.

Rival destruction should affect that rival.

Nothing about either event should freeze the rest of the race.
